  "novel_hypothesis_tested": "L5 divides the map with a solid color-5 wall pierced by a single 2-row gap at tile rows 7-8, col 9, leading into a 3-sided pocket that opens west toward the bay. Unlike L3s fence, the wall is NOT socketable -- blocks cross by being physically carried through the gap. The winning economy is a FERRY-AND-RELAY: the player ferries the six east-side blocks to drop points at or west of the gap, and the single robot (which freely roams BOTH sides through the gap) shuttles every drop to the 8-slot bay. Three robot-behavior discoveries: (1) the robot can freeze indefinitely while parked adjacent to a pickable block (observed 35 consecutive no-op presses), and STEALING its locked target unfreezes it instantly -- yet the same block at the same tile was picked up cleanly later, so the freeze is state-dependent, not block-specific; (2) when the player blocks its carry path head-on in the 1-tile corridor, the robot may ABANDON its cargo in place and re-path; (3) the robot greedily re-targets the nearest loose block at all times, so player drops can and should be used to steer its work queue.",
  "narrative": "Replayed the 237-action verified prefix (re-confirming the L4 candidate en route). Episode 1 (recon): confirmed the gap is passable both ways, measured the L5 timer drain at ~0.51 cells/action (~125 actions/episode -- the roomiest level yet), discovered the robot freeze + steal-unfreeze mechanic, and lost the episode to an ACTION5 pickup/drop toggle fumble while facing a carried blocks ghost (3/6 placed). Episode 2: near-miss at 5/6 -- a mid-corridor robot interception led to a desynced sequence that briefly UN-placed an already-delivered block; the last block was never fetched. Episode 3 (fumble-proofed pure-ferry script): player ferried all six blocks to gap-side drop points, robot made every bay deposit; five placed by step 594, and the budget cap landed with the sixth deposit 2-4 robot-presses away. The handed-over candidate appends a parity-safe pump tail to fund those presses. All hard constraints respected; no win claimed without the gate.",
  "l5_gotchas": [
    "The wall is solid and NOT socketable; the only crossing is the 2-tile gap at rows 7-8, col 9.",
    "The robot roams both sides through the gap and does all bay deposits reliably; the optimal player role is pure ferry to gap-side drop points.",
    "NEVER press ACTION5 while facing an adjacent block or carried ghost unless you intend to toggle pickup/drop -- two episodes were damaged by toggle fumbles (one un-placed a delivered block).",
    "The robot may abandon cargo mid-corridor if the player blocks it head-on; use the two gap rows as one-way lanes (player row 8, robot row 7 or vice versa).",
    "Steal-unlock: if the robot parks adjacent to a block without extracting for many presses, pick its target up yourself -- it re-targets instantly.",
    "Bay col-3 slots fill first and wall off col-2 access from the east; col-2 slots must be approached via col-1 (outside the bay border) with a ghost-east carry, or left to the robot.",
    "L5 timer drain ~0.51 cells/action (~125 actions/episode); post-GAME_OVER reset restores the exact fresh L5 entry and preserves the L4 checkpoint (verified field-by-field)."
  ],
